🚽 Test case: no-initializer variant of the grammar-boundary check --
🚽 `skibidi x;` (no initializer, scalar void) reaches a parse-time check
🚽 in lang.y that rejects declaring a variable with type void via YYABORT,
🚽 rather than waiting for semantic_visit_declaration() (which is
🚽 exercised by semantic_error_void_variable_declaration.brainrot).
🚽 This prevents creating an invalid declaration AST node and cleanly
🚽 aborts parsing without hard exit(1) in create_default_node().
🚽
🚽 Exercised here as a separate parse-time rejection path.
🚽
🚽
skibidi main {
    skibidi x;
    bussin 0;
}
